content.text:
# Folders tree panel — full implementation report

## 0. THE key finding first (this explains almost everything else you asked about)

`FoldersPanel` has two completely different render paths gated by its `embedded` prop, and **the app only ever calls it with `embedded` set to `true`**:

- `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/desktop/desktop-app-shell.tsx:360-402` — the only call site of `<FoldersPanel …>` in the whole repo (confirmed via repo-wide grep), and it passes `embedded` (shorthand for `true`) at line 401.
- Because `embedded` is always true, `FoldersPanel`'s `sectionContent` (in `/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/features/notes/navigation/ui/folders-panel.tsx:144-181`) always takes the `embedded ? (...)` branch (lines 148-172), which renders `<SidebarFileTreeNode>` (a shadcn/ui `Sidebar*` + Tailwind based component), **not** `<TreeNode>`/`<TreeRow>` (the dnd-kit + hand-rolled `app.css` component that `renderTreeNodes()` at line 90 builds).
- `FeedPanel` (`/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/features/notes/navigation/ui/feed-panel.tsx:209-238`) always renders `<TreeNode>` directly, wrapped in a `feed-navigation-tree` class, and passes `feedMode` down into `TreeRow`/`NavNoteRow`.

**So "Folders" and "Feed" are not the same component with different props — they are two structurally different implementations**, sharing only the underlying data shape (`NavigationNode`/`TreeItem`). This is why hover, font, and indentation all differ: it's not a couple of CSS tweaks, it's two parallel rendering stacks:

| | Feed | Folders (what's actually on screen) |
|---|---|---|
| Component | `TreeNode` → `TreeRow` / `NavNoteRow` | `SidebarFileTreeNode` |
| Styling | hand-written CSS in `app.css` (`.item-row`, `.tree-pane .item-row`, etc.) | Tailwind utility classes via shadcn `sidebar.tsx` (`SidebarMenuButton`, `SidebarMenuSubButton`, `SidebarMenuSub`) |
| Drag-and-drop | `useDraggable`/`useDroppable` from `@dnd-kit/core` wired in `TreeRow`/`NavNoteRow` | **none** — `SidebarFileTreeNode` has no dnd-kit hooks at all (its own doc-comment at `sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx:41` literally says "without drag-and-drop") |

The dnd-kit machinery you asked about in point 6 (`useDragDrop`, `dnd-tree.ts`, `tree-dnd.ts`, the `DndContext` in `desktop-app-shell.tsx:410-418`) is fully wired and functional, but currently has **no draggable folder rows to attach to** in the live UI, because the only mounted folder-tree renderer (`SidebarFileTreeNode`) never calls `useDraggable`. (Feed rows do call `useDraggable`, but `FeedPanel` passes `draggable={false}` — see feed-panel.tsx:235 — so even there it's inert.) Worth flagging to whoever owns this, since it may be an accidental regression from a refactor rather than intended behavior.

---

## 1. File map

```
apps/desktop/src/features/notes/navigation/
  ui/
    folders-panel.tsx        — FoldersPanel: renders SidebarFileTreeNode (embedded=true) or TreeNode (embedded=false, currently unused)
    feed-panel.tsx           — FeedPanel: always renders TreeNode, feedMode=true
    tree-node.tsx            — TreeNode: recursive renderer shared by Feed and by FoldersPanel's dead non-embedded branch
    tree-row.tsx             — TreeRow: folder row for the TreeNode stack (dnd-kit draggable/droppable)
    nav-note-row.tsx         — NavNoteRow: note row for the TreeNode stack
    sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx — SidebarFileTreeNode: the ACTUAL renderer used on screen for Folders (shadcn Sidebar/Tailwind, no DnD)
  model/
    types.ts                 — NavigationNode / TreeItem / FlattenedItem / Projection
    notes-tree-model.ts       — buildVisibleNavigationItems, selectPreviewSourceNotes, rename helpers
    tree-ops.ts               — pure tree ops: build/insert/remove/reorder, drop-target parsing
    dnd-tree.ts               — buildTree/flattenTree/getProjection (dnd-kit-sortable-tree derived)
    tree-dnd.ts               — dropId()/ROOT_ID/EdgeSnap type
  hooks/
    use-drag-drop.ts          — useDragDrop: drag start/move/over/end handlers for folders + notes
    use-keyboard-navigation.ts — arrow-key nav for both nested and flat modes
    use-feed-keyboard-navigation.ts
    use-pane-shortcuts.ts
  state/
    use-notes-tree-state.ts   — owns tree/expanded/treeData/flatItems/orderedIds, shouldNestNotesInNavigation
    use-notes-tree-actions.ts
    notes-tree-context.tsx
apps/desktop/src/shared/ui/sidebar.tsx   — shadcn Sidebar primitives actually driving Folders' look
apps/desktop/src/app/app.css             — hand-written CSS actually driving Feed's (and dead-code Folders') look
apps/desktop/src/desktop/desktop-app-shell.tsx — wires DndContext, FeedPanel, FoldersPanel, keyboard handlers
apps/desktop/src/app/hooks/use-tree-interactions.ts — handleFolderClick / handleFolderContextMenu
apps/desktop/src/shared/lib/selection.ts — computeRangeSelection (shift/cmd-click logic, shared by both trees)
```

---

## 2. Folders panel UI — full read

`/home/sprite/type/apps/desktop/src/features/notes/navigation/ui/folders-panel.tsx` (199 lines, read in full). Key excerpt, the actually-active branch:

```tsx
// lines 144-181
const sectionContent = (
  <div className={embedded ? "pane-section sidebar-folders-section" : "pane-section"}>
    {sectionTitle ? <div className="pane-section-title">{sectionTitle}</div> : null}
    {renderDroppablePaneBody(
      embedded ? (
        <SidebarMenu className="sidebar-filetree-menu">
          {treeData.length === 0 ? <div className="empty">No folders yet.</div> : null}
          {treeData.map((node) => (
            <SidebarFileTreeNode
              key={node.id}
              node={node}
              selectedIds={selectedIds}
              selectedNoteIds={selectedNoteIds}
              showNotesAsChildren={showNotesAsChildren}
              expanded={expanded}
              onSelect={onSelect}
              onToggle={onToggle}
              onNoteSelect={handleNoteSelect}
              onNoteContextMenu={handleNoteContextMenu}
              notePreviews={notePreviews}
              renamingFolder={renamingFolder}
              ...
            />
          ))}
        </SidebarMenu>
      ) : ( /* dead code path: <TreeNode> list, never reached */ )
    )}
  </div>
);

if (embedded) {
  return sectionContent;
}
```

Note: even the `useDroppable({ id: dropId(ROOT_ID, "inside") })` root drop target (lines 74-76, 116-142) is still wired regardless of `embedded`, but since child rows aren't `useDraggable`, nothing can ever be dragged into it.

### The real row renderer: `sidebar-file-tree-node.tsx` (full file read above, 188 lines)

Folder row:
```tsx
<SidebarMenuItem>
  <Collapsible open={isExpanded} className="group/collapsible">
    <SidebarMenuButton isActive={selectedIds.has(node.id)} className="sidebar-filetree-button" asChild>
      <div className="sidebar-filetree-button-inner" onClick={...} onContextMenu={...}>
        {hasNestedItems ? (
          <button type="button" className="sidebar-filetree-toggle" onClick={...}>
            <ChevronRight className={`sidebar-filetree-chevron${isExpanded ? " is-open" : ""}`} />
          </button>
        ) : (
          <span className="sidebar-filetree-toggle-spacer" aria-hidden />
        )}
        <Folder />
        {isRenaming ? <input className="rename-input sidebar-filetree-rename-input" .../> : <span>{node.name}</span>}
      </div>
    </SidebarMenuButton>
    {!isRenaming && node.noteCount ? <SidebarMenuBadge>{node.noteCount}</SidebarMenuBadge> : null}
    {hasNestedItems ? (
      <CollapsibleContent>
        <SidebarMenuSub>
          {notes.map((note) => (
            <SidebarMenuSubButton key={note.path} asChild isActive={selectedNoteIds.has(note.path)} size="md">
              <button type="button" className="sidebar-filetree-note-button" onClick={...} onContextMenu={...}>
                <File />
                <span>{preview?.title || note.name}</span>
                {preview?.isRecording ? <Mic size={12} className="sidebar-filetree-note-mic" /> : ...}
              </button>
            </SidebarMenuSubButton>
          ))}
          {node.children.map((child) => <SidebarFileTreeNode key={child.id} node={child} ... />)}
        </SidebarMenuSub>
      </CollapsibleContent>
    ) : null}
  </Collapsible>
</SidebarMenuItem>
```

This is the exact JSX rendered for the Folders panel today.

---

## 3. Tree model (`notes-tree-model.ts`) and traversal (`tree-ops.ts`)

`TreeItem` (types.ts:13-20):
```ts
export type TreeItem = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  children: TreeItem[];
  noteCount?: number;
  notes?: NoteEntry[];
  collapsed?: boolean;
};
```
`NavigationNode` (types.ts:5-11) is the same shape minus `collapsed`, used by both Feed buckets and Folders as a common contract.

`buildTreeItems` (`tree-ops.ts:8-16`) turns the backend `FolderNode` (real filesystem folder tree) into `TreeItem[]` recursively — this is what makes "Folders" the *real* user tree vs. Feed's synthetic date buckets (built by `feed-tree-model.ts`, not covered here since you didn't ask about it in depth).

Traversal/mutation helpers you'll want for reference:
- `flattenTreeData`/`flattenTree` (tree-ops.ts:25-38, dnd-tree.ts:35-52) — depth-first flatten with `depth`/`parentId`, used to build `orderedIds` (flat top-to-bottom order) for shift-click ranges and arrow-key nav.
- `findParentAndIndex`, `getNodeById`, `removeNodes`, `insertNodes` (tree-ops.ts:94-191) — pure, immutable tree surgery used by `useDragDrop`'s optimistic reorder.
- `parseDropTargetId`/`DropTarget` (tree-ops.ts:193-218) — decodes `drop:<id>:<inside|before|after>` ids produced by `dropId()` (tree-dnd.ts:7).
- `buildVisibleNavigationItems` (notes-tree-model.ts:36-77) — flattens the tree into a flat `{type: "folder"|"note", id, parentId}[]` list **only when `shouldNestNotesInNavigation` is true**, respecting `expanded`; this is what `use-keyboard-navigation.ts` walks for Up/Down/Left/Right when notes are nested inline.

---

## 4. Row rendering — hover / selected / shift-click, and full-width question

### 4a. Feed (`TreeRow`/`NavNoteRow`, actually rendered) — `app.css`

```css
/* app.css:433-444 (base, shared by both stacks in theory) */
.item-row {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  padding: 4px 10px; padding-right: 72px;
