`feed-navigation-tree` is added only by `FeedPanel` (`feed-panel.tsx:209`: `className="pane-body tree-root feed-navigation-tree"`). Because `.item-row` is `display:flex` (a block-level box), its width is already 100% of its container by default even without the explicit `width:100%;box-sizing:border-box`, so that particular declaration is close to a no-op — the practically meaningful Feed-only difference is the **hover/selected color** (`var(--sidebar-accent)` = `oklch(0.967 0.001 286.375)`, a near-white neutral tinted gray with `--sidebar-accent-foreground` text color swap) vs. plain Folders-stack hover (`#f7f9fb`, static gray, no foreground color swap). Both are visually subtle/light, but Feed's changes text color too, which reads as more "designed."

### 4b. Folders (`SidebarFileTreeNode`, actually rendered) — Tailwind via `sidebar.tsx`

