## 8. Shared hooks used by Folders

- `hooks/use-drag-drop.ts` — see §7.
- `hooks/use-keyboard-navigation.ts` (full file read, 461 lines) — `useKeyboardNavigation` returns `handleNotesKeyDown` and `handleFoldersKeyDown`. `handleFoldersKeyDown` (170-421) branches on `shouldNestNotesInNavigation`:
  - Nested mode (198-320): walks the flat `visibleNavigationItems` (folders+notes interleaved) for Up/Down, and handles Left/Right as expand/collapse or "enter/exit" folder semantics (mirroring Finder/VS Code tree behavior), calling `scrollIntoViewIfNeeded` against `[data-folder="…"]`/`[data-note="…"]` selectors — note both `TreeRow` (`data-folder={node.id}`, tree-row.tsx:97) and `SidebarFileTreeNode`'s underlying DOM would need to expose those same `data-*` attributes for this to keep working; **`SidebarFileTreeNode` does not set `data-folder`/`data-note` anywhere**, so `scrollIntoViewIfNeeded` calls against the Folders panel are currently no-ops (another consequence of §0 you may want to check).
  - Flat mode (322-420): walks `orderedIds` for Up/Down and `visibleItems`'s `children`/`parentId` for Left/Right.
- `hooks/use-pane-shortcuts.ts` — global-ish shortcuts (font size, new note, lock, etc.) gated on which pane last had focus.
- `hooks/use-feed-keyboard-navigation.ts` — Feed-only variant of the above, delegated to from `handleFoldersKeyDown` when `activeNavigationTab === "feed"`.
- `state/use-notes-tree-state.ts` — owns `tree`, `expanded`, `treeData` (via `buildTreeItems`), `flatItems`/`orderedIds` (via `flattenTreeData`), `parentById`, `renamingFolder`, and computes `shouldNestNotesInNavigation = notesListMode === "nested"` (line 83) from the appearance store's `notesListMode` setting.
- `app/hooks/use-tree-interactions.ts` — `handleFolderClick`/`handleToggle`/`handleFolderContextMenu`, all delegating selection math to `computeRangeSelection` (§4c).
